  "details": "- CVE-2026-6464: teach psql to skip in-line data after a COPY ... FROM STDIN that fails\n  before PGRES_COPY_IN, so the data is no longer executed as SQL\n- CVE-2026-6471: restrict logical decoding output plugins to the new\n  output_plugin_libraries parameter.  NOTE: this is a deliberate default-deny\n  change, matching upstream and RHSA-2026:67491.  Installations using a\n  third-party output plugin (for example decoderbufs/Debezium) must add it to\n  output_plugin_libraries in postgresql.conf and reload before logical\n  replication slots can be created again.  Audit with:\n  SELECT DISTINCT plugin FROM pg_replication_slots WHERE plugin IS NOT NULL;\n- CVE-2026-16239: cross-check the output row type of a portal running EXECUTE\n  or FETCH\n- CVE-2026-18408: do not perform backquote expansion on the argument of psql's\n  \\unrestrict command",
